     "question": "What is rainwater harvesting? Explain its methods and importance.",
     "marks": 3,
     "type": "short",
     "probability": "high",
     "answer": "Rainwater harvesting is the collection and storage of rainwater for later use, primarily to recharge groundwater and provide water for various purposes. Methods include: 1) Rooftop Rainwater Harvesting: Rainwater from rooftops is collected in tanks or pipes and directed to recharge pits or stored for use. 2) Surface Runoff Harvesting: Rainwater from surfaces like roads and open grounds is collected in ponds or tanks. 3) Subsurface Dams: Built underground to store rainwater and prevent evaporation. Importance: It reduces pressure on groundwater, mitigates floods, provides water during scarcity, improves water quality, and promotes sustainable water management."
