     "answer": "Rainwater harvesting is the collection and storage of rainwater for future use. The different methods of rainwater harvesting are: 1. Rooftop rainwater harvesting: This involves collecting rainwater from rooftops and storing it in tanks or underground reservoirs. 2. Surface runoff harvesting: This involves collecting rainwater from the surface and storing it in tanks or ponds. 3. Recharge wells: This involves directing rainwater into wells to recharge groundwater. 4. Check dams: These are small dams constructed across streams to collect rainwater and recharge groundwater. 5. Percolation tanks: These are ponds constructed to collect rainwater and allow it to percolate into the ground, recharging groundwater."
